      "content": "GENERAL information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d2ed7145-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement is subject to revision without prior notice. Please check with a counselor every semester to obtain current information about possible changes in the agreement. To learn more about the courses and programs offered at Sonoma State University or the General Education and Upper-division requirements for each major please refer to the university catalog at: http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/",
      "contentHtml": "This agreement is subject to revision without prior notice.  Please check with a counselor every semester to obtain current information about possible changes in the agreement.  To learn more about the courses and programs offered at Sonoma State University or the General Education and Upper-division requirements for each major please refer to the university catalog at: <a href=\"http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/</a>"
    },
    {
      "id": "9bca7645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "important transfer information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "78797445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Transfer students may only transfer the equivalent courses for PSY 250 Introduction to Psychology, PSY 280 Introduction to Research Methods and Math 165 Elementary Applied Statistics for the major. All courses for the major must be taken for a grade if this is offered, and must be passed with a grade of C or better.",
      "contentHtml": "Transfer students may only transfer the equivalent courses for PSY 250 Introduction to Psychology, PSY 280 Introduction to Research Methods and Math 165 Elementary Applied Statistics for the major.\nAll courses for the major must be taken for a grade if this is offered, and must be passed with a grade of C or better.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "4f1b7745-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Associate degree for transfer information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3e2f7445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "The AA-T in Psychology (SB 1440 degree) has been deemed a \"similar\" degree to the Psychology, B.A. at Sonoma State. Students transferring to SSU with an AA-T in Psychology are advised to complete all available articulated major requirement and support courses before transfer. It is also recommended that students complete the American Institutions (US-1, US-2, US-3), and Seawolf Studies Graduation requirements before transfer.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>The AA-T in Psychology (SB 1440 degree) has been deemed a \"similar\" degree to the Psychology, B.A. at Sonoma State. Students transferring to SSU with an AA-T in Psychology are advised to complete all available articulated major requirement and support courses before transfer. It is also recommended that students complete the American Institutions (US-1, US-2, US-3), and Seawolf Studies Graduation requirements before transfer.</p>"
    }
  ],
